In article <1993Feb26.125154.1@acad3.alaska.edu> fxmcs@acad3.alaska.edu (Milo Sharp) writes:
>   I'd like to see some of Saberhagen's Swords put in..  some would be too
>powerful (Shieldbreaker, Mindsword) but others, such as Townsaver, Stonecutter,
>and Dragonslicer would work easily...

	First off, I don't really see the point in adding Grayswandir in the
first place.  I mean, Zelazny's stories are great, but the sword is
superfluous, we already have silver arrows and Wereslayer, why another one?
Or does it have additional powers that I am not aware of?
	As for Saberhagen's 12 Swords, it's funny, I brought this up with a
friend and we talked about it and found lots of pros/cons.  But implementing
them shouldn't be too hard...but sort of worthless.
	Shieldbreaker wouldn't be that powerful.  Mindsword...yes.

	Shieldbreaker:  Destroys other weapons.  Of course, otherwise a
		worthless weapon.  Remember you CANNOT sheath Shieldbreaker
		when you are being attacked.  So once the weapon is
		destroyed, you are fighting hand to hand.  Remember that
		Shieldbreaker passes through the flesh of any unarmed
		creature without damaging it.  Actually rather pointless
		since the majority of creatures in Nethack don't carry
		weapons.
	Townsaver:  What can you defend?  Your pet?  Again, a pretty
		pointless power.
	Stonecutter:  Ok, this would be nice.  A combined weapon/pick axe.
	Woundhealer:  So, when wielding it, you are a nurse.  You are also
		invincible if you stick it through your body.  Too powerful.
	Dragonslicer:  We already have Dragonslayer.  It's redundant.
	Doomgiver:  Justice?  What sort of justice is there in Nethack?
	Soulcutter:  Who knows?  It's powers haven't really been outlined
		that great.  I guess it would make all monsters on the level
		weaker.
	Wayfinder:  It can find things.  Supposedly Excalibur is going to
		have this power in the future (from WCST spoilers).  So it's
		redundant.
	Mindsword:  Too powerful, what does it do, make everyone on the level
		tame?
	Sightblinder:  Gives displacement(?) or invisibility.  Whoopee.
	Coinspinner:  Acts like a luckstone.  How exciting.
	Farslayer:  Great, a one-shot weapon.  It would be funny though.
		"Throw what?"
		"a - a longsword named Farslayer"
		"You spin around...-more-"
		"Whom do you wish to slay?  Moloch"
		"You scream his name and release Farslayer. -more-"
		"Farslayer flies off and disappears...-more-"
		"A great cry of pain shakes the entire dungeon...-more-"
		"You feel that your quest will now be easier."
		Two turns later...
		"You hear your name being screamed by the ex-High Priest of
		  Moloch...-more-"
		"Farslayer appears before you and pierces you through the
		  heart...-more-"
		"You die."

	So, essentially, while it would be neat to see them, they are pretty
much unnecessary in Nethack.

